  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">Survival mode: play without your USB</h2>

  <p>The USB is not coming back before your set. Stop troubleshooting. The goal now is only this: <strong>music comes out of the speakers when it's your turn.</strong></p>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <li><strong>Ask the DJ before or after you.</strong> Borrow their USB, or ask around the venue for anyone with tracks. DJs help DJs — this happens to everyone.</li>
    <li><strong>Play from your phone.</strong> Ask the sound tech for a cable into a spare channel on the mixer (3.5mm or USB-C adapter). Streaming or local files both work.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the booth laptop.</strong> Many venues/residents keep one with Rekordbox — your USB may still read on a computer even if the player refuses it.</li>
    <li><strong>If another DJ is playing after you</strong>, ask to swap slots and use the extra time.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="question">Did you find a way to play?</p>

